​1. Overview


​Market POS ("we," "our," or "us") provides a point-of-sale, product catalog, and sales tracking application designed for retail, market, and commercial register operations. This Privacy Policy explains what information the app handles, how it is stored, and how you can manage or delete your data when using Market POS on Android and Google Play.


​2. Information We Collect and Process


​Depending on how you configure and use the app, Market POS may process the following categories of information:




​Business & Register Configuration Data: Store or business name, POS theme and display preferences (such as theme preset, accent color, font scale, screen scale, and selected currency such as USD, EUR, JPY, XCD, etc.), and tax/register settings.


​Sales, Inventory & Transaction Records: Product quick-keys, stock availability indicators, cart items, order subtotals, estimated taxes, amounts due, daily summaries, sales tracker metrics, and historical sales records stored for register operations and reporting.


​Account & Cloud Backup Information (If Cloud Account Features Are Used): If you register for or sign into a POS cloud account to back up or synchronize data, we may process account details such as your store/business name, email address, and authentication credentials/verification codes needed to create and protect your account. (If you use the app strictly offline/locally without creating a cloud account, this data remains on your device.)


​Device & Diagnostic Information: Basic device/app state and crash or build diagnostics required for Android compatibility, local database operation, and app stability.




​Market POS does not intentionally collect sensitive personal categories such as biometric templates, government IDs, or payment card numbers directly inside the POS register unless explicitly integrated with a separate payment processor.


​3. How Data Is Stored and Used


​We use your information strictly to operate and improve Market POS:




​Local Device Storage: Register settings, product catalogs, and sales history are stored locally on your device (including local database storage such as Room and local preferences) so your point-of-sale workflows function reliably and persist across app restarts.


​Cloud Backup & Sync (When Enabled): When cloud backup/account features are used, data is used to authenticate your account, back up POS records, and restore or sync store data.


​App Functionality & Support: Configuration settings ensure consistent currency formatting, layout scaling, and reporting across screens (such as Cart Stream, Quick-Keys, Sales Tracker, and Sales History).




​4. Data Sharing and Third-Party Services


​We do not sell your personal or business data to third parties. Data may only be processed or shared in the following limited circumstances:




​Service Providers / Infrastructure: Cloud hosting, authentication, or Google Play distribution services used to deliver and maintain the app.


​Legal Compliance: When required by applicable law, regulation, or valid legal process.




​5. Data Retention and Deletion




​Local Data: Sales records, catalog items, and display preferences remain on your device until you clear app data, uninstall the app, or delete records within the app.



​Account / Cloud Data: If you have a cloud account or backed-up data, you can request account or data deletion by contacting us at [Your Support Email].





​6. Security


​We take reasonable technical and organizational measures—such as restricting access, using encrypted connections where data is transmitted, and keeping local register data isolated within the app's storage—to help protect your store and transaction information against unauthorized access or alteration. No method of electronic storage or transmission is 100% secure.


​7. Children's Privacy


​Market POS is a commercial point-of-sale and business management tool intended for merchants, cashiers, and store managers, not for children under the age of 13 (or the applicable age of digital consent in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.


​8. Changes to This Privacy Policy


​We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time as features or legal requirements evolve. Any updates will be posted at the Privacy Policy URL with a revised Effective Date.


